{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374703-exalted-i-m-gonna-get-real-weird-with-it-a-thread-on-remixing-exalted-s-system","id":1374703,"title":"Exalted: I'm gonna get real weird with it - a thread on remixing Exalted's system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-13T21:52:50-07:00","id":1374703,"title":"Exalted: I'm gonna get real weird with it - a thread on remixing Exalted's system","content":"Summary: I'm going to remake the entire Exalted system (<b>not</b> fluff) within a week, based on weirdest mechanic ideas suggested on the first page of this thread. Kindly start blasting ideas.<br /> <br /> Post starts here -<br /> <br /> So! I've been doing game design for a fair bit for the last few years, but recently I got stuck in a slump. On top of that, I'm (voluntarily) confined to my apartment for a week due to the current health crisis. All of this has compounded to a bit of a downer episode. So, I figured - <i>let's do something entirely pointless, for fun.</i> I can't seem to be able to make a game for a purpose, so maybe I can make something for no purpose.<br /> <br /> I thought of this challenge to myself: pick an established game with an intricate setting, and remix it. But not the setting part. The setting part is the limiter, the difficulty, the challenge. I intend to remix the mechanics that support and engage with the setting. It's one thing to make a generic system and a system-agnostic setting and say &quot;hey, play this with this!&quot; Designing a game for the intent of accentuating and highlighting a setting is something else!<br /> <br /> Now, what better candidate than Exalted? So I'm gonna get <i>real weird</i> with it.<br /> <br /> But it's no fun if I do this on my own - I want this to be an interaction in itself! So ITT, I'll regularly post updates on Weird Exalted development. Furthermore, I would like ask you all to give me Weird Mechanics Ideas. I plan to pick a few from the first page and base the entire Weird Exalted system off of it. Like, I don't know, why not use bagua/hexagrams instead of d10s? Exalted without a Storyteller? No randomness generators? Each Exalted type uses different game mathematics? (Don't suggest this... but now that I think about it, <i>do</i> suggest it). Ideas like these!<br /> <br /> So please share your weird (but still workable and fertile in the context of Creation) mechanic ideas here! I'll see what I can do with them.<br /> <br /> While this is something fun for fun's sake and I won't playtest it, I want the final product to be <i>theoretically feasible</i>. I recognize that this whole idea is a balancing act between ludicrousness and seriousness! The intent is to practice game design skills, to make a game system that powerfully engages with Creation and Beyond, and to examine Exalted by flipping it inside out. It's <i>not</i> for wackiness! I'll have to see how that goes, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T22:06:03-07:00","id":1374706,"title":"","content":"Three words: <i>Color-coded cubes</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T22:07:26-07:00","id":1374707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374703-exalted-i-m-gonna-get-real-weird-with-it-a-thread-on-remixing-exalted-s-system?p=1374706#post1374706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three words: <i>Color-coded cubes</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid cubes are already thoroughly explored in the context of Exalted. But I could always explore them differently... Perhaps it's color-coded cubes of <i>different sizes</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T22:38:46-07:00","id":1374709,"title":"","content":"Charm usage is based on syllable count.<br /> <br /> In order to use charms on your turn, you have to roll a certain number of successes on a certain amount of dice. The number of successes determines how many syllables long the names for the charms you use can be.<br /> <br /> For example, if I wanted to use Hungry Tiger Technique, I would need to roll six successes to use up to six syllables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T02:36:39-07:00","id":1374725,"title":"","content":"Variable difficulty.<br /> <br /> So you're trying to convince a guard to let you pass - maybe he has a helpful intimacy you don't know about, maybe he has a good reason to stop you.<br /> <br /> Or you are arm wrestling a stranger. Maybe she's all bluster. Maybe she's the god blooded daughter of the god of arm wrestling.<br /> <br /> After setting the difficulty and rolling, draw a combat modifier card from the Gloomhaven monster deck and apply it to the successes rolled. A null is an automatic botch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T03:24:57-07:00","id":1374733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>szp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374703-exalted-i-m-gonna-get-real-weird-with-it-a-thread-on-remixing-exalted-s-system?p=1374707#post1374707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid cubes are already thoroughly explored in the context of Exalted. But I could always explore them differently... Perhaps it's color-coded cubes of <i>different sizes</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>You figure out the particulars, I just saw the thread and immediately knew what the first reply had to be is all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T20:13:38-07:00","id":1374871,"title":"","content":"A luck pool where players can give themselves &quot;bad luck&quot; by narrating an adverse circumstance and removing dice then later give themselves &quot;good luck&quot; by narrating a beneficial circumstance and adding those removed dice. In order to force meaningful decisions, the removed dice are rolled anyways and only added to the luck pool if their removal turned what would have been a success into a failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T06:31:36-07:00","id":1374912,"title":"","content":"When a player establishes a sufficiently important/lasting/interesting thing in the &quot;canon&quot; of a game, that is noted down on their character sheet. This can be introducing a fact or crafting something, but there's a lot more it could be; writing a text with Linguistics or composing a song with Performance; using social influence and roleplay to create an organization; making a sorcerous working; blasting a scar into the landscape with Death Ray; brokering a trade deal. An OOC meme or running gag qualifies, as do houserules. If the game is such that players write parts of the world, that counts. These things are your Wonders. Note that not everything you make is a Wonder; the group must agree that it is such. Wonders can be jointly held if that makes sense, and different characters/players may be determined to hold different facets or aspects of a Wonder.<br /> <br /> Wonders act like the Sobriquet Merit in that you can boost a stunt involving them, but you can also develop Wonder Evocations for them. These are essentially custom Charms derived from the Wonder's establishment. They're not tied to a physical Artifact like a normal Evocation would be; if a Wonder is established by you creating an Artifact, that Artifact will have normal Evocations, while Wonder Evocations will instead key off the <i>act</i> of creating that Artifact and may enhance your capacity to do similar things. Characters and players thus accrue unique powers based on their contribution to the IC and OOC canon of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T07:13:20-07:00","id":1374916,"title":"","content":"-Whenever you roll dice, you may turn individual dice around to change their value to one you like more. Each time you turn a die, gain 1 automatic point of Limit.<br /> <br /> -All conflicts between Exalts must be resolved via friendly competition, such as a strongman contest, a fishing competition or a rap battle. Breaking this edict in any way has the same consequences as breaking an Eclipse pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T08:55:22-07:00","id":1374927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>szp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374703-exalted-i-m-gonna-get-real-weird-with-it-a-thread-on-remixing-exalted-s-system#post1374703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! I've been doing game design for a fair bit for the last few years, but recently I got stuck in a slump. On top of that, I'm (voluntarily) confined to my apartment for a week due to the current health crisis. All of this has compounded to a bit of a downer episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks. Commiserations.<br /> <br /> Maybe... X no of descriptors instead of attributes, positive and negative (e.g. quick-witted, hulking, seductive, striking). Dice pools determined by score and how many of these are interestingly evoked in the stunt description in the eyes of the ST. Each descriptor also adds a bonus, so 'deadly' might mean you double 10s on damage.<br /> <br /> Would be an administrative nightmare mind, a unique dice pool for every roll...<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, every shaping effect requires you to model it with play-dough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}